content.body:
A class groups data members and member functions. Objects are often created directly as local variables, without new:

class Dog {
public:
    Dog(std::string name) : name_(name) {}
    std::string bark() const { return name_ + " says woof"; }
private:
    std::string name_;
};

Dog rex("Rex");

The constructor Dog(std::string name) initializes name_ in its initializer list (after the :). A local object like rex is destroyed automatically at the end of its block, which runs its destructor, written ~Dog().

